.TH mnnn-model-edit 1  "mnnn-model-edit 2.10.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
mnnn\-model\-edit \- Change a model\*(Aqs draft (renames, then changes, drops, adds and moves), its name or description. \-\-apply applies the draft right away
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmnnn model edit\fR [\fB\-\-add\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-change\fR] [\fB\-\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-drop\fR] [\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR] [\fB\-\-rename\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-\-move\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-description\fR] [\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIMODEL\fR> 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change a model\*(Aqs draft (renames, then changes, drops, adds and moves), its name or description. \-\-apply applies the draft right away
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-add\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Add a field: NAME:TYPE [constraints]. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Muninn home directory (default ~/.muninn)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-change\fR \fI<SPEC>\fR
Change a field: NAME[:TYPE] [constraints] (what is not given stays). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-db\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Database file (default <home>/storage/muninn.database)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_DB\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-drop\fR \fI<FIELD>\fR
Drop a field. Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-\-non\-interactive\fR
Never prompt; missing values are errors
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_NON_INTERACTIVE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rename\fR \fI<OLD:NEW>\fR
Rename a field, OLD:NEW (values are kept). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
More output (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-move\fR \fI<FIELD:N>\fR
Move a field, FIELD:POSITION (1 is first). Repeatable
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but errors and requested data
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_QUIET\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Rename the model (right away; not versioned)
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Answer yes to every confirmation
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_YES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR

.TP
\fB\-\-theme\-mode\fR \fI<THEME_MODE>\fR
Override the theme mode for this run
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
light
.IP \(bu 2
dark
.IP \(bu 2
system
.RE
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBMUNINN_THEME_MODE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-apply\fR
Apply the draft afterwards
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIMODEL\fR>

.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH VERSION
v2.10.0
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBmnnn\fR(1)
